cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Epistemic Futures Corpus: what the Epistemic Futures Summit's attendees have written and said, in their own words"
authors:
  - family-names: Priem
    given-names: Jason
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6187-6610"
    affiliation: OpenAlex
abstract: >-
  A plain-text corpus of everything each attendee of the MIT Epistemic Futures Summit
  (September 23–24, 2026) has written or said and published openly on the internet from 2005
  onward — papers, books, blog posts, op-eds, interviews, talks, and public social-media posts —
  one file per item with source URLs, plus speaker-attributed transcripts of talks and a markdown
  copy of the summit's public website. Compiled with AI agents (Claude) working to a written
  collection spec, with help from Jason Priem. Collected texts remain their authors' and
  publishers'; the corpus's own contributions are CC0.
keywords:
  - corpus
  - text
  - Epistemic Futures Summit
  - scholarly communication
  - AI and knowledge
  - OpenAlex
